# DexJoCo evaluation standard

## Official policy eval (S0 / B1 / future methods)

When reporting DexJoCo task success (e.g. `water_plant`), use this protocol—not a one-off fresh seed range:

1. **Seeds**: `0` through `49` (50 seeds). Colloquially “seed 0–50”; count is **50** so that `50 × 4 = 200`.
2. **Repeats**: run the same seed set **4 independent times** (4 full passes).
3. **Budget**: **200 episodes total**.
4. **Metrics**: report **mean and variance** of success rate across the 4 runs (each run = success rate on seeds 0–49). Also keep the pooled `successes/200` for reference.
5. **Control protocol** (unless the user overrides): blocking, `replan_steps=24`, `max_env_steps=1000`, no domain randomization / dynamics randomization.

Do **not** treat a single contiguous block of 200 fresh seeds (e.g. `seed=28704217`, `n=200`) as the official score.

Smoke / debug evals may use fewer episodes or other seeds; label them clearly as non-standard.

## Stack (mandatory for all DexJoCo / DEWO v2)

There is **no 384 / min-max training or eval plan**. Every infer / eval / collect / continue-train / DEWO v2 path — including mixed-S0 `water_plant` — uses the open-source recipe (fold_glasses DEWO v2 / FastWAM-infer-in-DexJoco).

| Piece | Pin / path |
|---|---|
| Inference repo | `FastWAM-infer-in-DexJoco` (`scripts/eval_dexjoco.py`, `FastWAMDexJocoPolicy`) |
| FastWAM code | `third_party/FastWAM_pin_45d8e14` @ `45d8e14…` |
| DexJoco | `third_party/dexjoco` @ `8d23b0f…` |
| Model config | `OPEN/configs/fastwam_dexjoco.yaml` → **224×224**, **z-score** |
| Stats | `OPEN/artifacts/<task>/dataset_stats.json` (or mixed `artifacts/mixed_5task/dataset_stats.json`); **not** `data/<task>_fastwam/meta` min-max |
| Text (base) | `OPEN/artifacts/<task>/*.t5_len128*.pt` (CFG/FAST suffixes may add a dedicated cache, still T5/Wan) |
| Expert data | `data/dexjoco/dexjoco_lerobot_datasets/<task>` |
| Control (default) | `action_horizon=32`, `replan_steps=24`, `nfe=10`, `max_steps=1000` |

Weights under `checkpoints/dexjoco/<task>_fastwam` are **release ckpts** for this stack (name only). Do not pair them with local async `s0_bundle` packing.

**DEWO v2** (unspecified = **scratch**) entrypoints pin this stack (`TASK=` + `INIT=` + session env, no per-task copy):

- Collect / prepare / train / CFG eval: `scripts/dewo_v2/{collect_opensource_4x50,prepare_pair_eve,train,eval_cfg_official_4x50}.sh` (`TASK`, `INIT=scratch|s0`, `GPUS`, `DEWO_HYDRA_OVERRIDES`)
- Task identity: `scripts/dewo_v2/tasks.py`
- Data/task: generic Hydra `dexjoco_dewo_v2_offline_b1_jump_fast_full_1e-4` (scratch) or `dexjoco_dewo_v2_offline_b1_jump_fast_full_s0` (from S0). **There is no LoRA recipe.** `INIT=lora` and `*lora*` Hydra task names are removed.

**DEWO v9** is a frozen-S0 VideoDiT-encoded value head on the v6 pool/mix (`INIT=s0 DEWO_VERSION=v9`). Freeze the whole pretrained MoT. Train the same text-side K/V adapter **and** an MLP on pooled current-obs VideoDiT tokens (adapter off, S0 base text). Mix is still `ε_cfg = ε_0 + g w (ε_+ − ε_0)` (subtract **base**, not v7 fail). **D0** = one episode per 4/4 all-success seed. **D+** = full-horizon success stitch (prefix `[0,t)` + continuation). **D_fail** = fail cliff `[t, M+24)` only, not 33-frame crops. Value target is the progress return `G_t=γ^{T-t}` on success and `G=0` on the fail cliff — do **not** train \(V\) toward a floor near the event. Gate is a **drop-edge once-fire** (`V_{t-1}-V_t > δ`); **no** `v_high` floor and never `σ(V−τ)`. `text_cfg_scale=1` / `g=0` is 本体. Hydra: `dexjoco/dexjoco_dewo_v9_offline_b1_jump_fast_uncond`. Checkpoint format stays `dewo_v5_uncond_adapter_v1` with `recipe: v9`. This is not LoRA and not the 384 / min-max recipe.

**DEWO v8** is a frozen-S0 value head on the v6 pool/mix (`INIT=s0 DEWO_VERSION=v8`). Freeze the whole pretrained MoT. Train the same text-side K/V adapter **and** a small MLP on pooled current-frame VAE latents. Mix is `ε_cfg = ε_0 + g w (ε_+ − ε_0)` (subtract **base**, not v7 fail). **D0** = one episode per 4/4 all-success seed (not a random 15 of 166). Gate is a **drop-edge once-fire** (`V_{t-1}` high and `V_{t-1}-V_t > δ`), never `σ(V−τ)`. `text_cfg_scale=1` / `g=0` is 本体. Hydra: `dexjoco/dexjoco_dewo_v8_offline_b1_jump_fast_uncond`. Checkpoint format stays `dewo_v5_uncond_adapter_v1` with `recipe: v8`. Falsify with leave-one-pair-out before official 4×50. This is not LoRA and not the 384 / min-max recipe.

**DEWO v7** is the pair-CFG mainline (`INIT=s0 DEWO_VERSION=v7`). Same frozen-adapter shell and D0/D+/D_fail shuffle pool as v6, but the guided mix is `ε_cfg = ε_0 + w · (ε_+ − ε_-)`. Freeze the whole pretrained MoT. Train adapters on **video and action** text-side cross-attn **K/V** only. Checkpoint format stays `dewo_v5_uncond_adapter_v1`; distinguish via `recipe: v7`. **D0** = full success episodes (base text, video+action BC). **D+** = pair success-event windows (action BC, ` Successful execution.`, v5 dropout `0.9,0,0.1`; video **base**, identity lock). **D_fail** = pair failure events (**action** BC on ` Failed execution.` to define `ε_-`; no video BC; no action residual lock; video pinned to base). Drop aux_success copies. Hydra: `dexjoco/dexjoco_dewo_v7_offline_b1_jump_fast_uncond`. Infer: `text_cfg_scale=1` = 本体 bypass (report first). Mix `w=1` is `ε_0+(ε_+−ε_-)`, **not** `ε_+`. Default guided `w=1.2`. Gate energy is NFE0 exec RMS of `(ε_+ − ε_-)`. `τ=q_{0.10}(E+)` (`recall=0.90`); disable adaptive if `FPR0>0.05`. Eval yaml must set `cfg_failure_prompt`. This is not LoRA, not DPO, and not the 384 / min-max recipe.

**DEWO v6** is the v5 frozen-adapter shell plus v2 pair events and D0 alignment (`INIT=s0 DEWO_VERSION=v6`). Same freeze and adapter wrap as v7. Residual is still `ε_+ − ε_0`; D_fail is video BC only. Keep as the same-data **对照**. Hydra: `dexjoco/dexjoco_dewo_v6_offline_b1_jump_fast_uncond`. Infer: `w=1` = 本体 bypass (report first); default guided `w=1.2`. Gate: NFE0 exec RMS `E>τ` else mix=0, energy is `RMS(ε_+ − ε_0)`. `τ=q_{0.10}(E+)` (`recall=0.90`); disable adaptive if `FPR0>0.05`. `ADAPTIVE_CFG_TAU=auto` reads `RUN_DIR/adaptive_cfg_tau.json`. Do not treat `tau=0.05` as a v6 prior. This is not LoRA and not the 384 / min-max recipe.

**DEWO v5** is frozen-uncond + bounded residual (`INIT=s0 DEWO_VERSION=v5`), not Ho joint CFG training. Freeze the whole pretrained MoT. Train adapters on **video and action** text-side cross-attn **K/V** only. Video text is always the S0 **base** prompt; action text gets CFG dropout `0.9,0,0.1`. Video residual is trained by **action loss** plus identity lock (`identity_lock_lambda=0.1`); `lambda_video=0`. Do not wrap Q or O. Do not train on failure / aux_success (all-primary batches). Save adapter-only `dewo_v5_uncond_adapter_v1`. CFG: `ε_cfg = ε_base + w · (ε_adapter − ε_base)` with adapter **off** + base = 本体, adapter **on** + action success / video base = adapter. Hydra: `dexjoco/dexjoco_dewo_v5_offline_b1_jump_fast_uncond`. Eval: `CKPT` may be the adapter file; backbone from `BACKBONE_CKPT` or `config.resume`. Use v5 only for ordinary-success CFG without recoverability events. This is not the removed LoRA recipe.

Other launchers:

- Official open-source 4×50: `scripts/dexjoco/eval_opensource_4x50.sh` (`TASK`/`TASKS`, `GPUS`, `WAIT_IDLE`)
- Baseline suite: `scripts/dexjoco/eval_all_opensource_baselines_4x50.sh`

If a path still points at `data/<task>_fastwam` or `*/meta/` min-max, **align** it to the table above. Do not refuse-and-stop, and do not recreate the 384 recipe.

## Rollout / data collection (S0 and later)

Collection seeds must **not overlap** the official eval set `0..49`.

Use a disjoint seed range (or an explicit high base seed) for S0/B1 rollout datasets so training data does not contaminate the held-out eval seeds.

Collection for DexJoCo / DEWO v2 stays on the open-source recipe (224 / z-score / artifacts / replan=24).

## Agent behavior

- Default to the open-source 224 / z-score stack for eval, infer, collect, open-loop width, continue-train, mixed S0, **DEWO v2**, **DEWO v5**, **DEWO v6**, **DEWO v7**, **DEWO v8**, and **DEWO v9**.
- For a frozen-S0 VideoDiT value head that drop-edge-gates sparse CFG (mix still `ε_0+g w(ε_+−ε_0)`), launch `INIT=s0 DEWO_VERSION=v9`. D0 is one episode per 4/4 all-success seed. Pair data is full-horizon success stitch + fail cliff. Train \(V\) to `G_t=γ^{T-t}` (fail=0); do **not** floor \(V\) near the event. Gate is drop-only (`V_{t-1}-V_t > δ`), no `v_high`. Do **not** gate with `σ(V−τ)`. `text_cfg_scale=1` / `g=0` is 本体.
- For a frozen-S0 VAE value head that drop-edge-gates sparse CFG (mix still `ε_0+g w(ε_+−ε_0)`), launch `INIT=s0 DEWO_VERSION=v8`. D0 is one episode per 4/4 all-success seed. Do **not** gate with `σ(V−τ)`. `text_cfg_scale=1` / `g=0` is 本体. Official 4×50 only after the leave-one-pair probe.
- For CFG post-train that must keep the pretrained base bit-exact **and** put recoverability contrast into the guided residual, launch `INIT=s0 DEWO_VERSION=v7` (frozen adapter; D0 alignment + D+ Successful action BC + D_fail Failed action BC as `ε_-`; mix `ε_0+w(ε_+−ε_-)`; `text_cfg_scale=1` first).
- For the same-data 对照 that still subtracts S0, launch `INIT=s0 DEWO_VERSION=v6`.
- For CFG post-train that must keep the pretrained base bit-exact on ordinary success (no recoverability events), launch `INIT=s0 DEWO_VERSION=v5`.
- Default to the official 4×50 protocol when the user asks to “测一下 / evaluate / benchmark” S0, B1, or later schemes on DexJoCo.
- Launch via env knobs on the generic scripts (`scripts/dexjoco/eval_opensource_4x50.sh`, `scripts/dewo_v2/*.sh`). **Do not** copy a task `.sh` or bake `GPUS` / `RUN_DIR` / a dated experiment into a new launcher.
- If currently running a non-standard / wrong-stack eval, stop or finish only as the user prefers, then schedule the correct stack + 4×50 protocol.
- When summarizing results, prefer `mean ± var` (or `std`) over the 4 runs, not only a single pooled rate.
